te":1786060800.0,"result_type":"web","source_name":"SuperGrail","attribution":"supergrail.com"}]},{"type":"search_result_group","domain":"www.wired.com","entries":[{"type":"search_result","url":"https://www.wired.com/gallery/best-travel-adapters/","title":"8 Best Travel Adapters (2026): 20+ Models Tested | WIRED","snippet":"","ref_id":{"turn_index":215474,"ref_type":"search","ref_index":4},"pub_date":1789084800.0,"result_type":"web","source_name":"WIRED","attribution":"www.wired.com"}]},{"type":"search_result_group","domain":"www.tomsguide.com","entries":[{"type":"search_result","url":"https://www.tomsguide.com/best-picks/best-portable-chargers","title":"The best power banks for travel, work, and emergency charging - tested in the real world","snippet":"This tested guide ranks six portable chargers for travel, work, emergencies, and camping. The CUKTECH 30 is the overall winner, offering a huge 40,000mAh capacity, 140W output, four wired ports, wireless charging, and airline approval, though its 2.5-pound weight limits portability. The $49 Ugreen Nexode 12,000mAh is the budget choice, combining 100W output with a compact design and battery display, but simultaneous charging reduces power significantly. Statik\u2019s SmartCharge Pro is recommended for travel because it includes built-in cables, magnetic wireless charging, international plug adapters, pass-through charging, and a 15,000mAh capacity. The five-ounce INIU Pocket Rocket is the most pocketable option, while Sharge\u2019s IceMag 2 provides actively cooled MagSafe charging, a kickstand, pass-through charging, and 10,000mAh capacity. For camping or outages, the 256Wh Anker PowerHouse 521 supplies AC, car, USB, lighting, and optional solar charging. The guide advises choosing at least 10,000mAh for frequent or multi-device use, prioritizing USB-C Power Delivery, versatile ports, and charging speeds of 30W or more.","ref_id":{"turn_index":215474,"ref_type":"news","ref_index":12},"pub_date":1789552911.0,"result_